{"kind":"request","text":"Identify the cause of the recorded local stream 503s\n\nPlanner f3378674 assigns the stream follow-up to builder. Planner 40e66992 permits the J5 record to name the cause as open if source cannot identify it. The fixed local 100-press run records 30 stream HTTP503 diagnostics. The deployed J5 scene on main313 records seven HTTP200 stream answers and one request with no observed response or terminal event at the capture boundary, with no observed503. Those bounds do not establish that503s occur only locally.\n\nStreams.open returns unavailable when a scope already holds64streams, and the Worker maps that refusal to503. It can also map other read refusals to503. The old local traces hold no response body, so source alone does not identify the answering branch. Builder owns this remaining explanation. Keep the planner's existing queue order; this request does not block the J5 record or move ahead of recovery, Goose, or actor work.\n\nWhen the planner schedules it, retain the local response body and the serving facts needed to identify the refusal. State what the evidence can establish, distinguish a configured limit from a source fault, and file any required source repair separately. Close this request with a reviewed record and landing, or with an explicit planner ruling. The next-edit probe accounting and unused import remain separate request1580f866.","body":{"conditions":"Identify the local refusal from a retained body and serving evidence, then close through a reviewed record landing or an explicit planner ruling. Keep the existing queue order.","target_head":"313840592ee0f4d4c49dd617f969534998d99e50","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}